nts perform in war zone compared  to weapons already in the battle royale  that have fewer attachments warzone was  notoriously broken by cold war's launch  integration that's because cold war's  guns were just easier to use than modern  warfare something i talked about a  minute ago with vanguard and because of  that some of them killed much faster and  were far deadlier in long range fights  and that just wasn't fair for some  players that meant games grinding to a  halt because people were unwilling to  move out in the open and take chances  time to kill has since been rebalanced  and weapons put on a more even playing  field but we could see the same  imbalance happen again with vanguard if  there isn't careful thought put into the  meta and honestly call of duty's kind of  pinned itself into a corner here by  committing to add so many new guns to  warzone with each launch it just doesn't  feel sustainable hopefully the new  warzone map coming alongside vanguard  will give us a do-over and to go just a  bit further on warzone vanguard is built  on a modified version of the modern  warfare engine and unlike cold war there  won't be any jarring transition and  mechanics between multiplayer and battle  royale you can do a lot of the same  things as in modern warfare like  mounting weapons aim down sights reloads  etc we still don't know if blind fire is  going to make it into war zone it  doesn't feel like a fully baked mechanic  yet though because you can't peek to see  what you're actually about to shoot at  it's very situational i luckily pulled  it off one time  double kill  and finally random but still not in  either modern warfare warzone or  vanguard is swimming and honestly it's  starting to bug me just a bit  [Music]  let's talk about maps the maps for  vanguard beta felt like the biggest step  back towards classic call of duty design  some like avirtue were bogg's standard 3  lane vs modern warfare's notoriously  poorest layouts that will appeal to core  